# Production build environment.
#
# Vite reads `.env.production` whenever the mode is production, which `vite
# build` is by default. So the Static Web Apps workflow picks these up with no
# extra flags.
#
# Two things follow from that:
#
#   1. These values are BAKED INTO THE BUNDLE at build time. They cannot be
#      changed afterwards. The Static Web Apps "Environment variables" blade
#      will not help — those are runtime settings for managed functions, and
#      nothing here is read at runtime. Changing a value means a new build.
#
#   2. Everything here ships to the browser and is readable by anyone who opens
#      devtools. Never put a real secret in a VITE_ variable.
#
# This file is NOT gitignored (.gitignore covers .env, .env.local and
# .env.*.local only), which is deliberate — the values below are public by
# nature and belong in version control. Anything you would rather not commit
# goes in `.env.production.local`, which is ignored and takes precedence.
#
# The GitHub Actions workflow can also override any of these: Vite's `loadEnv`
# copies VITE_-prefixed process env over the file values.

# ============================================================================
# TEMPORARY — THIS BUILD SERVES SAMPLE DATA, NOT A REAL BACKEND
# ============================================================================
#
# `movead-api` has no reachable hostname yet and `movead.in` is not registered,
# so there is no API for this bundle to talk to. Rather than ship a portal that
# throws on load, the mock is switched on: every screen renders and is
# clickable, and every figure on it is invented.
#
# Nothing on screen says so. Do not demo this to a customer as live data, and
# do not point a custom domain at it while this block is in place.
#
# TO GO LIVE, change exactly three lines below:
#
#   VITE_APP_ENV      staging -> production
#   VITE_USE_MOCK_API true    -> false
#   VITE_API_URL      -> the real API origin
#
# `VITE_APP_ENV` has to move too, not just the mock flag: `usesMockApi()`
# refuses to mock at all once `appEnv === 'production'`, so leaving it as
# `production` here would put the crash straight back.
# ============================================================================

# Unused while the mock is on, but `env.ts` throws at import time if it is
# empty, so it has to be a real URL. Replace with the `movead-api` Web App's
# Default domain from its Overview blade — Azure now issues a unique hostname,
# so it will look like https://movead-api-<suffix>.<region>-01.azurewebsites.net
# rather than https://movead-api.azurewebsites.net, which does not resolve.
VITE_API_URL=https://icy-mushroom-043c2f900.6.azurestaticapps.net

# `staging`, not `production`, only so the mock is allowed to run. See above.
VITE_APP_ENV=staging

# The one that matters most. See the warning block above before changing it.
VITE_USE_MOCK_API=true

# One origin, matching the `web` bundle that production deploys: advertisers at
# the root, operations under /admin, drivers under /driver. Only used where an
# absolute address is unavoidable, such as a link in an email.
#
# These are the Static Web App's default hostname. Once custom domains exist
# (DEPLOYMENT.md Phase 11) they become https://app.movead.in — which is also
# what makes login work, because the session cookie is sameSite=strict and a
# portal on *.azurestaticapps.net talking to an API on *.azurewebsites.net is
# cross-site, so the browser drops it.
VITE_ADVERTISER_URL=https://icy-mushroom-043c2f900.6.azurestaticapps.net
VITE_ADMIN_URL=https://icy-mushroom-043c2f900.6.azurestaticapps.net/admin

# Only the mock reads this. Against the real API the server decides and the
# login page follows — but keep it true so the two never disagree on screen.
VITE_ADMIN_MFA_REQUIRED=true

# Optional. Leave empty to disable Sentry rather than removing the line.
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=

# Browser Maps key. Public by definition, so the protection is the restriction,
# not the secrecy: restrict it by HTTP referrer, and enable only Maps
# JavaScript API and Places API. Do not enable Directions or Distance Matrix.
#
# Left empty here on purpose — the workflow supplies it from the
# VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY repository secret, which overrides this line. Maps
# panels stay blank until that secret exists; nothing else breaks.
VITE_GOOGLE_MAPS_API_KEY=AIzaSyDT-t-f7eiDp6zVbCGS0yFzparEjWbidmk
